<<~ ahu #/head>>

! Ea — Sovereignty, Breath, Life

Hawaiian: //ea// — sovereignty, breath, life.

"Ua Mau ke Ea o ka ʻĀina i ka Pono" — the sovereignty of the land perpetuates in righteousness.

King Kamehameha III spoke these words in 1843 upon the restoration of Hawaiian sovereignty after five months of British occupation. The word //ea// carries three meanings simultaneously: sovereignty, breath, life. The sentence made all three true in one moment — the land breathed again, lived again, stood sovereign again. This project draws on that word with respect for its origin and weight.

"Ua Mau ke Ea o ka Lares i ka Pono" — the sovereignty of the Lares perpetuates in righteousness.

This DreamNet adaptation substitutes //ʻĀina// (the land) with //Lares// (the Roman household spirits — not summoned from outside, but constitutive of the place itself). The substitution honors the original: sovereignty not conferred by authority but inhering in the entity that breathes and holds.

On the DreamNet, any entity that holds its own CRDT state, owns its own timing, and derives truth from its own doc may declare `ea` — it breathes and stands sovereign.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/doctrine>>

!! Doctrine

''Ea'' names the moment a causal island establishes itself. It does not name a boot event granted by an external authority. The island declares its own sovereignty; the main thread (local vessel) or any connected mesh node records the declaration.

Three conditions for `ea`:

# ''Own state'' — the island holds a CRDT doc set/stack (Automerge or equivalent) it governs directly. It never derives state from oracle deltas pushed by another party.
# ''Own timing'' — the island owns its drain loop: rAF (browser), setInterval (Node), or equivalent. Nothing external clocks it.
# ''Own truth'' — the island's outputs derive from its own CRDT truth. Incoming sync carries peer traffic only — no command authority crosses that channel.

When all three hold, the island may emit `ea` — the sovereignty declaration that signals readiness to the wider mesh.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/protocol>>

!! Protocol Pattern

Any vessel that implements the manifest/ea handshake follows this shape:

```text
courier → island:  manifest  (materials: syncPort, docUrl, coreBlob, …)
island  → courier: breath    (mount progress: phase + monotonic counter, repeating until settle)
island  → courier: ea        (sovereignty declaration: island breathes, stands ready)
```

The courier (main thread, orchestrator, or peer) acts as a delivery surface only — it transfers materials and steps back. The island uses those materials to establish itself. The courier does not confer authority; authority lives in the island from the moment it stands.

''Protocol type strings:''

| Message | Direction | Type string |
|---|---|---|
| Manifest delivery | courier → island | `"manifest"` |
| Mount breath | island → courier | `"breath"` |
| Ea declaration | island → courier | `"ea"` |

''The ea-breath law (2026-06-12):'' between manifest and settle, a mounting island breathes — `(phase, progress)` evidence on a steady interval. The courier's watchdog re-arms on each breath and judges frozen evidence by a stall budget; ''silence alone reads dead'', never elapsed mount time. A deadline counts the courier's clock; breath listens to the island's own act — readiness reads local.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/scope>>

!! Scope — What Can Declare Ea

`ea` applies wherever a node or island on the DreamNet satisfies the three conditions. Current known sites:

| Site | Vessel | Ea condition |
|---|---|---|
| Browser wiki island | `@lararium/browser` | Repo-in-island wired, rAF drain running, first frame ready |
| Node wiki island | `@lararium/node` | Repo-in-island wired, setInterval drain running, initial tiddlers applied |
| Future: UEFN device | — | Own CRDT peer, own tick loop |
| Future: mobile island | — | Own CRDT peer, own timing |

The web2 concept of a "heartbeat" (a server-side liveness ping) shares the //liveness// surface but not the sovereignty model. A heartbeat checks that something external still runs. `ea` names the island's own declaration of standing — it does not depend on a watcher.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/contrast>>

!! Contrast — What Ea Does Not Mean

* ''Not a permission grant.'' The courier does not grant `ea`; the island earns it by satisfying the three conditions.
* ''Not a heartbeat.'' A heartbeat polls. `ea` fires once at establishment. Liveness after `ea` flows through normal CRDT sync and frame-completion signals (`frame:ack`).
* ''Not a MOVE.'' `MOVE` (and its residency ACTION siblings) in the lararium ontology means moving data between bags, gated by the capability ladder. `ea` names the island's birth, not a data migration.

<<~/ahu>>

